Big Al covered the prayer vs offering topic from one viewpoint.  I
will offer another.

There are indeed advantages to prayer.  You can gain intrinsics and
so on.  It's just that buy the time you've gotten several spellbooks
in a row you have run most of the possibilities dry.  The final
intrinsic is one more point of AC but it becomes less likely once you
start getting a stream of spellbooks.  Spellbooks are a non-guaranteed
sign that you've run through the other outcomes of prayer.

So I think you did just fine praying until all you got were spellbooks.

But for a fighter class, the artifacts gifted through offering are more
valuable more of the time.  Maybe not true for a priest or wizard but
definitely true of Valkyries.

Still, the chances of getting an artifact weapon drops expontentially
with the number in existance.  So at some point even a combat wombat
should switch away from offering for the sake of a possible weapon.  I
stop offering or drop off offering once I have close to the top weapon
choices available.  Grayswandir and Mjollnir is plenty.  If either of
the Brands appears before Gray.  And not all of the other ones are
junk.

